## What problem(s) does this PR solve?

- Continues https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965
- Continues https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118214

Speeds up `RefCounted` creation by ~15%.

`RefCounted` is now constructed with an initial refcount nearly everywhere. We can make use of this by actually initializing the refcount to 1 instead of updating it post-init.

## Additional information

Future PRs should update `ClassDB::instantiate` and remove internal uses of `init_ref` because those are still assuming the old system. That will speed those up too.

I also took the opportunity to rename `refcount_init` to `negative_refcount`. It was never a refcount and the name misrepresented it.

### Benchmarks

Benchmarks show a ~15% speedup for `RefCounted` creation. This does not translate to GDScript, likely because of overhead and possibly because it uses other creation paths.
There is also a ~5% regression for the `ClassDB::instantiate` path. This is because this path is not using the "already has a refcount at init" semantics. A follow-up PR will have to address this.

> **Note:** Benchmarks were AI generated.

